## Usage Advice

- **Example:** ex:packetGroundingLogicBatch0 a gmeow:AuthoringPacket ; gmeow:packetSourceSlice \<…/slices/logic\> ; gmeow:packetBatch 0 ; gmeow:packetCoversTerm logic:Rule , logic:ConfInconsistent \.
- **Use when:** Use to give an author or reviewer everything needed to author or review one subdomain batch \(~25 terms\) of a slice in one place, and to drive downstream glossary\-coverage and candidate\-review tooling that reasons over which terms are grounded in which language or external ontology\.
- **Avoid when:** Do not author packet individuals by hand or treat a packet as a source of truth: a packet is a derived projection, regenerated from the slices and the bundle\. Do not read fr/zh labels 'through' a term\-equivalence record — translations are JOINed from the per\-slice \.po catalogs, never carried on the equivalence\. Do not silently omit a missing translation or a short exemplar set; record the absence explicitly\.
- **How to use:** Produced by the slice\-brief projection as a single consolidated sparse fold at generated/briefs/authoring\-packets\.nt \(all slices' packets in one file\), and on demand for a single slice by \`gmeow slice brief \<dir\>\`\. Partition a slice's terms with \-\-axis / \-\-batch, then read each covered term's definition, axioms, neighbours, exemplars, and grounding coverage\. The RDF projection is sparse: it materializes only the present fr/zh/external incidences and summarizes coverage in the per\-attribute margins \(gmeow:packetFrPresent / packetFrAbsent, packetZhPresent / packetZhAbsent, packetExternalMapped / packetExternalAbsent\) — read those counts to see how much grounding is missing, or the on\-demand JSON / text view for the explicit per\-term absences\.

